{
 "fps": 30,
 "totalFrames": 1760,
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "He told eight armed outlaws the bank safe was locked. It wasn't.",
   "from": 0,
   "to": 88
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Northfield, Minnesota, eighteen seventy-six. The James-Younger gang rides into a quiet town.",
   "from": 91,
   "to": 228
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Inside the bank sits acting cashier Joseph Heywood.",
   "from": 231,
   "to": 310
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "speaker": "outlaw",
   "text": "Open the safe! Now!",
   "from": 313,
   "to": 401
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "speaker": "heywood",
   "text": "I can't. It's on a time lock.",
   "from": 405,
   "to": 482
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "The outlaws believe him. One steps into the vault, and Heywood throws the heavy door on him.",
   "from": 485,
   "to": 614
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "speaker": "outlaw",
   "text": "My arm! Get me out!",
   "from": 618,
   "to": 655
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "In the chaos, teller Alonzo Bunker bolts out the back door. A bullet hits his shoulder, but he keeps running.",
   "from": 659,
   "to": 796
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Outside, the town has noticed. A hardware merchant grabs his rifle.",
   "from": 800,
   "to": 909
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "speaker": "townsman",
   "text": "Get your guns, boys! They're robbing the bank!",
   "from": 913,
   "to": 978
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "And inside, the outlaws are still waiting on a lock they think will never open.",
   "from": 982,
   "to": 1092
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "You see, a time lock is a clock inside the safe door. Once it's set, nobody can open it until the hour comes.",
   "from": 1107,
   "to": 1279
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "But Heywood's clock had never been set. The safe was unlocked the whole time. One turn of the handle.",
   "from": 1283,
   "to": 1424
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Bullets fill the street. The gang flees with twenty-six dollars and seventy cents.",
   "from": 1428,
   "to": 1542
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Three outlaws were killed and three captured. The gang never recovered.",
   "from": 1546,
   "to": 1636
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Heywood paid for his bluff with his life. But the bank's money never left the safe.",
   "from": 1640,
   "to": 1736
  }
 ],
